& [SolutionIdentity] is the completed deterministic ecosystem prerequisite
  + [solution_uuid] is 4711c0b4-bfeb-4e29-abdd-333bca962cf4
  + [profile] is cantor-supervised-mock-loop/0.1
  + [status] is completed_and_boundedly_activated
  + [semantic_authority] is caller-supplied verified cantor_core execution
  + [agent_authority] is one deterministic commissioned mock cycle
  + [effect_authority] is none

& [MachineFormSolution] is strict and bounded
  + [forms] are participant address, authority grant, commission, work packet, acceptance criterion, envelope, expected response, candidate, review, decision, outcome, metrics, failure, and typed fault
  + [serialization] is deterministic Serde JSON with unknown struct fields denied
  + [text] is nonempty NUL-free and at most 4096 bytes
  + [collections] are ordered and limited to 256 profile-owned items
  + [digests] are lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256
  + [outcome] is replayable and cross-validates transcript payloads, core response, Observer review, decision, progress, and metrics

& [AuthoritySolution] is containment before delegation
  + [dimensions] are project, semantic operation, tool capability, data scope, and effect class
  + [intersection] can only retain values present in both grants
  + [work_packet] must be contained by the commission
  + [message] must be contained by commission and work packet
  + [phase_1] rejects every nonempty effect-class grant
  - never: infer effect authority from another dimension

& [TranscriptSolution] is append-only admitted evidence
  + [route] is principal to manager to Codex worker to Cantor participant to Codex worker to Observer to manager to principal
  + [context] is exact commission correlation and work-packet frame
  + [causation] requires an admitted predecessor that handed control to the sender
  + [response_contract] requires the declared next kind at or before its logical deadline
  + [replay] rejects duplicate message identity, idempotency identity, and equivalent semantic state
  + [budgets] bind message count, canonical serialized bytes, logical ticks, and call depth
  + [atomicity] is no index, metric, or transcript mutation before every gate passes
  + [fault_control] is out of band with the immutable accepted prefix; Phase 1 admits no fault envelope

& [AdapterSolution] is a deliberately narrow seam
  + [MockCodexAdapter] accepts exactly one bound work packet and one response bound to its emitted request
  + [FunctionCantorAdapter] calls one supplied executor and verifies the returned protocol response
  + [fixture] compiles and signs one real SOP document then executes one inspect-fabric request through cantor_core
  - never: call live Codex, a model provider, network, filesystem, process, notification, or effect surface

& [ObserverSolution] is deterministic no-effects review
  + [checks] are Honesty, Security, Protocol, AcceptanceCriteria, and EffectBoundary exactly once
  + [honesty] requires known criterion claims plus declared evidence and proof references
  + [protocol] requires a successful response that passes the core verifier
  + [acceptance] requires all work-packet criteria
  + [security] and [effect_boundary] require containment and no requested effect
  + [decision] accepts only a coherent all-pass review and otherwise revises without action
  - never: claim deterministic Phase 1 checks are model-based FacultyProgram execution

& [DeterminismSolution] is a fixed seven-message computation
  + [logical_ticks] are activation plus one through activation plus seven
  + [call_depth] is 0, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 0
  + [identities] derive from one caller-supplied semantic namespace
  + [fixture_outcome_sha256] is 2ef72ed3edf4bf58e80e24c5d86bea18572ba10324e27e02aacc63569cd78b3c
  + [termination] is first final decision or first typed fault
  - never: retry, recurse, revise automatically, spawn another worker, or execute an effect

& [NonclaimSet] is retained
  + [Codex] is a mock adapter rather than a live task or control API
  + [Observer] is mechanical validation rather than the seven compiled faculties
  + [proof_refs] prove declared presence and lineage rather than exterior artifact authenticity
  + [runtime] is in-memory and single-cycle rather than persistent, recoverable, notifying, or distributed
  + [routing] is deterministic protocol routing rather than learned neural routing
  + [manager] is a machine-form role boundary rather than an autonomous Shaliach agent
